Package: ustravel911study
Title: U.S. Travel Around September 2001
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("Benvenuteo", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "79843566+Benvenuteo@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Reproducible portfolio analysis of monthly U.S. air, rail and road
    travel, with pre-event temporal validation, forecasting and transparent
    observed-versus-forecast comparisons. This is an analysis project,
    not an installable R package.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.4.0)
Imports: fpp3, fable, fabletools, feasts, tsibble, dplyr, tidyr, tibble,
    readr, ggplot2, ggtime, lubridate, generics, distributional, jsonlite,
    digest, patchwork, knitr, rmarkdown, renv, urca, testthat
